From: Yannick Serafini <yannick.serafini@wifx.net>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:56:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Compute the MCU/SX130X drift mean over a truncated window

mcu_drifts[] feeds two consumers with opposite requirements. log_drift_stats()
derives drift_thres from a quantile of the window and must see outliers to
stay calibrated. sum_mcu_drifts, the mean of the same window, is a drift
estimate feeding the "Mean MCU drift" line, the rt_utcOffset correction and
ts_normalizeTimespanMCU(), which scales RefTime - and it must not. A unit
locked up at -914ppm was reporting its own pairing error as its TCXO rate and
scaling RefTime by it.

Filtering what is recorded would make the outlier detector ratchet down to
MIN_MCU_DRIFT_THRES; that variant was measured on target and rejected. Keep
recording every sample and truncate at the point of use: once drift_thres is
recomputed from the untouched window, average only the entries within it.
Keep the previous mean when the truncated set is empty.

Rationale, the rejected variant and its measurements:
doc/wifx/timesync-recovery.md

Signed-off-by: Yannick Serafini <yannick.serafini@wifx.net>
