+### The two statistics lines
+
+Emitted together, once per completed window of 20 samples:
+
+```
+[SYN:INFO] MCU/SX130X drift stats: min: +0.1ppm  q50: +0.4ppm  q80: +0.9ppm  max: +12.3ppm - threshold q90: +2.1ppm
+[SYN:INFO] Mean MCU drift vs SX130X#0: -0.4ppm
+```
+
+The first is unchanged and still reflects the full window, outliers included - that is what
+keeps `threshold q90` meaningful. The second is now the truncated mean, so during a lockup it
+no longer echoes the pairing error back at you. The two disagreeing by orders of magnitude
+while samples are being rejected is the expected picture, not a fault.
+
 ---
 
